---
import ArticleLayout from "@/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site.config";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title={`About ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={siteConfig.description}
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <p>{siteConfig.name} publishes editorial buying guides for {siteConfig.audience}.</p>
  <h2>Who is responsible for the editorial work</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are maintained by the {siteConfig.author.name}. The team reviews
    available product information, maps the buyer decision a page can actually
    help with, and names situations where a reader should not buy through a
    link.
  </p>
  <h2>What our pages can and cannot say</h2>
  <p>
    We separate listing information from editorial guidance. We do not claim
    hands-on testing unless a page says it was tested and explains that evidence.
    We do not publish invented prices, ratings, personal outcomes, or medical
    conclusions. Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> and
    <a href="/review-methodology/">review methodology</a> for the full process.
  </p>
  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not claim hands-on testing when it did not happen.</li>
    <li>We do not turn a brand claim into an independent finding.</li>
    <li>We do not rank a product simply because it has an affiliate link.</li>
    <li>We do not publish an empty category just to make the site look larger.</li>
    <li>We do not present changing price, stock, or merchant terms as permanent facts.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We explain our use of automation on the <a href="/ai-transparency/">AI transparency</a> page. It does not replace the editorial responsibility for published pages.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
